  "title": "Erdős Problem #271",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $A(n)=\\{a_0<a_1<\\cdots\\}$ be the sequence defined by $a_0=0$ and $a_1=n$, and for $k\\geq 1$ define $a_{k+1}$ as the least positive integer such that there is no three-term arithmetic progression in $\\{a_0,\\ldots,a_{k+1}\\}$.\nCan the $a_k$ be explicitly determined? How fast do they grow?",
